  "title": "Audi R8: First-Gen V8 Performance",
  "script": "Looking for supercar thrills without breaking the bank? The first-generation Audi R8 with its 4.2-liter V8 might be your perfect match. This naturally aspirated engine delivers 420 horsepower, launching you from 0 to 60 mph in just 4.6 seconds. ([ru.wikipedia.org](https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/Audi_R8?utm_source=openai)) Paired with Audi's quattro all-wheel-drive system, it ensures exceptional grip and handling. Compared to its V10 sibling, the V8 offers a more affordable entry into the R8 lineup, providing 90% of the experience at 60% of the price. ([automonitor.io](https://automonitor.io/blog/is-a-audi-r8-worth-buying/?utm_source=openai)) Plus, the V8's reliability and lower maintenance costs make it a practical choice for enthusiasts. With tuning, you can even push the V8's performance closer to the V10's territory. ([westracingshop.com](https://westracingshop.com/products/audi-r8-stage-1-tune?utm_source=openai)) So, would you choose the V8's value or the V10's raw power?",
